{
  "_README": "BUNDLE, not a single sci descriptor. Do NOT run `./sci --sim HELIOS`. sci applies every configuration to every workload in one descriptor (local_runner.py: `for config_key in configs`), so a lone descriptor can only do the full config x app matrix. This bundle instead holds one descriptor per optimal-tuning group so each app runs ONLY baseline + its own optimum (32 sims total, no sweep). Run the loop in `_run_loop`. Each `runs[]` entry is a complete sci descriptor; the loop writes it to json/<experiment>.json (gitignored: json/HELIOS_*.json) and runs sim/collect-stats/visualize. 12/16 apps beat baseline; the other 4 (rag_haystack, sssp_ego_fb, tc, toolformer) have no config that beats baseline, so they run at T65000 (least-aggressive best-attempt arm, ~baseline). Binary scarab_current = I-Fuse gitrev 563795f (opt). architecture \"in\" resolves to I-Fuse/src/PARAMS.in, which IS the Golden Cove config (no separate PARAMS.golden_cove needed). Data from /users/vedlaksh/helios_results/{STATE.json,SUMMARY.csv}.",

  "_run_loop": "cd /users/vedlaksh/scarab-infra && python3 -c \"import json,subprocess,pathlib; b=json.load(open('json/HELIOS.json')); [ (pathlib.Path('json/%s.json'%d['experiment']).write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)), [subprocess.run(['./sci',a,d['experiment']]) for a in ('--sim','--collect-stats','--visualize')]) for d in b['runs'] ]\"",

